    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field on the owner read model per the spec.\n\n**Changes (3 files):**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `riskFlag` boolean (read-only) property to the `Owner` schema, so `OwnerDto`/`setRiskFlag` regenerate at build time.\n\n2. **`RiskFlags.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, cohesive helper (`WMC_other \u2248 0`) that OR-combines the three existing building blocks:\n   - `PossibleDuplicates.matchId(...) != null` \u2014 possible (soft) duplicate\n   - `DisposableDomains.isBlocked(...)` \u2014 disposable-adjacent email domain\n   - `CityCapacity.approaching(...)` \u2014 city over its soft capacity\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.getOwner`** \u2014 one line: `ownerDto.setRiskFlag(RiskFlags.isRisky(...))`.\n\n**Structural-impact rationale:** All logic lives in a new isolated class that reuses the three pre-existing detectors, so no existing method grows and no complex class absorbs new branches. The only edit inside the large controller class is a single wiring line in `getOwner` (low CC), keeping the `WMC_other \u00d7 CC \u00d7 changed_lines` cost minimal.\n\nFull test suite: **1 test, 0 failures \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.**",
